+# US-08.5 – Optional email copy of the submitted answers
+
+Part of [Employee onboarding questionnaire](../feature.md), section [8. Completing and submitting the questionnaire](../feature.md#SEC-08-completion-and-submission).
+
+**As** new employee, **I want** to choose, when I submit the questionnaire, to email myself a copy of my answers exactly as I submitted them, **so that** I can look up what I entered myself instead of calling HR to ask
+
+Priority **P2** – HR asked for it because new employees keep calling to ask what they entered. That is a recurring support burden, but it blocks no registration, and the copy is optional. · Status: **inferred** · Sources: F-hr_email_copy-37cede, F-hr_email_copy-f75a41, F-hr_email_copy-029105, F-hr_email_copy-b67d2f, F-hr_email_copy-ab2538, F-hr_email_copy-6d2b5a, F-hr_email_copy-07f744, G-01, G-10, D-036
+
+> ⚠ Open questions affecting this section: [OQ-copy-email-retention](../open-questions.md#oq-copy-email-retention)
+Covers (details in [the section](../feature.md#SEC-08-completion-and-submission) and [information.md](../information.md)): Wants an email copy of the answers, Email address for the copy, Email copy for the employee
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- **AC-08.5.1 Copy offered at submission, optional**
+  - **Given** any employee at the end of the questionnaire
+  - **When** they submit
+  - **Then** Lonio asks whether they want an email copy of their answers (yes or no). The question is optional: the employee can decline or leave it unanswered and still submit
+  - _Sources: F-hr_email_copy-37cede, F-hr_email_copy-f75a41, G-10_
+
+  | Example | → | Wants an email copy of the answers | Checked |
+  |---|---|---|---|
+  | Any employee at submission (illustrative) | → | optional | ✅ |
+
+- **AC-08.5.2 Email address asked only when a copy is wanted**
+  - **Given** an employee at submission
+  - **When** they choose to receive a copy
+  - **Then** they type in the email address the copy goes to, and it is required. If they do not want a copy, no email address is asked
+  - _Sources: F-hr_email_copy-029105, F-hr_email_copy-b67d2f, G-01_
+
+  | Example | Wants an email copy of the answers | → | Email address for the copy | Checked |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|
+  | Wants a copy (illustrative) | yes | → | required | ✅ |
+  | Declines the copy (illustrative) | no | → | not asked | ✅ |
+
+- **AC-08.5.3 Copy contains the submitted answers exactly, nothing more**
+  - **Given** an employee who chose a copy and typed in an email address
+  - **When** they submit the questionnaire
+  - **Then** an email with their answers, exactly as submitted, is sent to that address. It contains no derived results (such as the insurance start date, the civil status for the pension fund or the tariff code) and no answers that were discarded on submission because they no longer applied
+  - _Sources: F-hr_email_copy-37cede, F-hr_email_copy-ab2538, D-036_
+
+  | Example | Wants an email copy of the answers | Email address for the copy | → | Email copy for the employee | Checked |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|---|
+  | Copy requested with an address (illustrative) | yes | new.employee@example.com | → | yes | ✅ |
+
+- **AC-08.5.4 No copy without the choice**
+  - **Given** an employee who declined the copy or left the question unanswered
+  - **When** they submit the questionnaire
+  - **Then** no copy is sent
+  - _Sources: F-hr_email_copy-f75a41_
+
+  | Example | Wants an email copy of the answers | → | Email copy for the employee | Checked |
+  |---|---|---|---|---|
+  | Declines the copy (illustrative) | no | → | no | ✅ |
+  | Leaves the copy question unanswered (illustrative) | – | → | no | ✅ |
+
+- **AC-08.5.5 Email address used to send the copy**
+  - **Given** an employee who typed in an email address for the copy
+  - **When** the copy has been sent
+  - **Then** the address has served its purpose. No receiving party needs it. Whether it is kept afterwards or recorded for HR is open (see OQ-copy-email-retention)
+  - _Sources: F-hr_email_copy-07f744, G-01_
+_Trace check: partial – AC-08.5.3 names 'the civil status for the pension fund' as a derived result, and the P2 priority is stated, but no cited fact backs either; the rest is supported._
+
+
